--- /dev/null
+++ b/test/numinous/README-sparse-prefill-fp8.md
@@ -0,0 +1,12 @@
+# sparse_prefill_fp8 (prototype, 2026-09-22)
+
+Triton sparse MLA prefill over the FlashMLA fp8 KV layout (512 fp8 nope | 4 fp32 tile scales | 64 bf16 rope) for
+small head counts, with -1 masked entries and optional per-row lengths, returning (o, lse base e). Purpose: DCP
+prefill without padding 8-16 heads to FlashMLA's 128-head tile.
+
+Measured on one B200 (`operations/modal/kernel_test.py` in numinous-inference): correct against the torch reference
+(max |o err| 5e-4 in bf16, lse exact, empty rows consistent). Speed at 4096 tokens x K=2048 x 8 heads: 6.0 ms per
+call (0.9 TB/s of gathered rows), split-K 8, BLOCK_N 64, 4 warps. The trtllm path TP8 runs is ~2.4 ms for the same
+work; FlashMLA head128 with padding is about where this kernel is. Next steps to close the gap: fp8 tensor-core dots
+(quantise q per row), TMA/cp.async row gathers with deeper pipelining, and fusing the owner filter for the DCP
+local-shard variant. Not wired into the backend yet.
